  "appeal_decision": null,
  "description": "The proposed works are confined entirely to the ground floor interior of the Givenchy retail premises and are limited to four specific zones within the existing store layout: Room 7: Removal of the existing pink metro tiles from both walls and flooring. Installation of a new timber parquet flooring, with new shelving and freestanding fixtures. Walls and ceilings surfaces will be prepared for repainting. Walls and ceilings to be painted. Existing lighting to be partially removed and replaced with new track lighting.\nRoom 7 (Fitting Room) - Removal of mirrors from both walls, doors and the ceiling. All wall, door and ceiling finished will be repaired and repainted. The pink metro floor tiles will be removed and replaced with new carpet. Existing fitting room benches will be replaced with new freestanding seating.\nLobby (Cash desk Area) - Removal  of pink metro tiles from walls and flooring. Installation of a new parquet flooring to match Room 7 and preparation of walls for repainting.\nRoom 3 - Removal of mosaic wall and ceiling tiles, preparation of surfaces for repainting. Painting the walls. Replacement of carpet as specified in the drawing.\n\nNo works are proposed to the building’s façades, basement, upper floors, or any areas containing original or listed architectural features. The proposals involve no changes to the internal layout, partitioning, or circulation routes, and do not require any structural alteration.",
